ne higher  consciousness that cease to exist when  it created the universe related concepts  such as pantheism and panentheism  similarly dictate that we are all  aspects of one universal being inside  the game of roy we open on a group of  teens hanging out at choi's grocery one  of the first signs we have that things  aren't as they appear is that all the  characters are voiced by justin roiland  doing variations on his morty voice this  is a playful jab at the entire show as  royland already voices pretty much every  character including all the ricks and  all the mortys as we learn holy's  characters are limited by stereotypical  knowledge held by mortys so it's  especially scathing that dorky morty's  version of being a cool kid amounts to  skaters doing rad tricks you can't name  one ollie or christ dare canyon morty  play goddamn tony hockey dweeb actually  seeing these various facets of morty's  personality personified across the  spectrum of the npcs reminds me a lot of  season three's rest and relaxation in  which morty's toxic essence was sucked  out of him leaving only the good parts  of him unfortunately with no doubt  embarrassment anger or other  quote-unquote toxic emotions that  version of morty becomes a mini patrick  bateman here we're seeing something  similar with each npc embodying a  specific part of what makes morty morty  and we're left to question how morty  will change if certain parts of him were  left behind this plot mostly follows  marta an aspect of morty that houses his  greatest potential to be a great  unifying leader rix roy has trouble at  first convincing the npcs that they're  all his grandson morty until marta  eventually rises to the occasion as a  figurehead for this cause marta comes  from morty's idea of a devoted jewish  family and she represents new age  thinking that questions religious  traditions as the morty ideology begins  to spread especially among the younger  generation within the game we start to  see little campaigns and slogans pop up  for the cause the sign on the door of  the grandson gathering says welcome  grandsons when the fuzz busts in to  arrest roy for doing religion wrong you  can see posters in the background that  read we're all grandsons and mortys  unite to be honest i was a little bummed  out that the npc morty's band song about  being part of the collective of  grandsons wasn't a full parody of smells  like teen spirit because that hello  hello  really got me excited there for a second  roy and marta eventually visit president  leland an old-fashioned and vaguely  southern version of morty that  apparently calls women things like honey  and pumpkin tits in his office you can  see pictures of what appears to be  abraham lincoln a fisherman james monroe  andrew jackson and george washington  hung in his office there's also the  painting buffalo ball grazing on the  prairie painted in 1830 by george  caitlin which actually hung in the oval  office during kennedy's presidency the  president explains that eight percent of  morty doesn't innately trust roy slash  rick because despite the fact that he's  been campaigning for 50 years to save  his mind he's never once said i love you  to any of them when marta confronts roy  about this he flippantly tells her that  he's willing to lose eight percent of  morty's consciousness because in the  grand scheme of things eight percent  isn't that terrible of a loss he argues  that eight percent of the snyder cut is  just batman dreaming i did some rough  math and it turns out that only 2.8 of  the snyder cut is batman dreaming but  funnily enough ign also did some math  and they found that 10.38  of the snyder cut is in slow-mo which  likely accounts for rick's slight  miscalculation because rick's so willing  to leave marta in her homeland behind  the morty npcs start a holy war between  the formerly peaceful involved countries  on their zoom call you can see the flags  of representatives from poland india  rwanda south africa cuba spain america  senegal china israel italy great britain  liechtenstein korea vietnam japan  pakistan new zealand switzerland canada  finland australia and brazil the npcs on  mardis side revolt desiring to live out  their lives within the game instead of  returning to the real world they end up  dividing into two factions loyalist of  acucratic randinistas whose symbol is  the letter r in honor of roy rick and a  star and ship representing rick's plans  to return the morty's home and stay  publican contra-sergeant confederates of  dedication of video game reality which  features an m for morty and marta the  game controllers symbolize their  dedication to staying within the  simulation one of the morty npcs can be  seen stealing toilet paper in the  apocalypse an all too familiar response  to impending global catastrophe after  decades of war choi's grocery has been  destroyed and marta's daughter informs  her mom that she's joining the other  side likewise larry begs marta to please  let him get on the spaceship that will  take him the other parts of morty back  to the real world and although marta  allows him to die inside the game she  realizes that she too is holding aspects  of morty hostage to her beliefs like her  father once did to her she finally  changes her mind and gives roy rick the  go-ahead to take the other npc morty's  home although rick swears that he got  all of morty out of the game it's  revealed after they leave by two arcade  employees that the roy game froze unable  to reset because roy died inside the  game shifting the storyline's focus to  an elderly marta living her best life  this means that that part of morty is  still trapped inside the game which  becomes apparent when he seems to trust  rick implicitly as they head off on  their next adventure it makes sense that  he's behaving like this like i said  earlier marta was clearly the part of  morty with independent thought and who  questioned rick's motives and decisions  and now that she's chosen to live inside  the game forever that part of morty is  absent irl although the employees make  it sound like arik purchased the machine  so that he could later extract this part  of morty i don't know they referred to  him as a rich old guy and i didn't know  that this dude was rich i mean  technically rick c137 has definitely  stolen bartered for or purchased a ton  of rare items over the years but i  refuse to trust an off-screen rick  because we didn't see him expressly ask  for the game let alone pick it up my  rogue's theory is that rick prime was  the buyer think about it he could  totally suck marta's morty out of the  game and upload it into his own morty to  rival our morty or worse he could hold  that part of morty hostage rendering him  useless to his chosen grandpa if this  looks familiar the roy machine is being  held in a storage center that's  reminiscent of hanger 51 from indiana  jones that's it for the breakdown but i  do have a little heads up for you guys  i'm going on vacation next week so my  very good best buddy mt is gonna take  the wheel for episode three i trust mt  with both my portal gun and my life and  i know he's gonna knock this next  breakdown out of the central finite  curve so please please please show him  some love i'll see you guys back here  for episode four so stay tuned follow me  on instagram and twitter whitneypuppy  follow new rockstars subscribe to new  rockstars for more analysis of  everything you love and thanks for  watching bye  [Music]  do  [Music]  you
 

